    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (71.41) anchor the LawDog lineup as our strongest plays, benefiting significantly from matchups against favorable arms in R. V\u00e1squez and Eric Lauer. Both players are seeing massive efficiency boosts due to sub-5.00 SP_xERA matchups and elevated batting orders; **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s projected move into the #3 hole provides a 6% efficiency lift, while **Bryson Stott** capitalizes on an 18% skill-gap advantage against the opposing starter. Additionally, **Lawrence Butler** (67.05) and **Tyler Freeman** (67.67) remain high-ceiling plays; despite some wind-in concerns for **Lawrence Butler**, both benefit from dynamic platoon advantages that keep them comfortably above our 60.00 \"Strong\" start threshold.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Masyn Winn**, who landed at 37.52, narrowly missing the cut against Nathan Eovaldi. While **Masyn Winn** typically offers the elite sprint speed we covet for our stolen base-starved 5x5 build, the combination of a high-end opposing starter and unfavorable wind conditions suppressed his efficiency score below the 40.00 floor. Similarly, **Jung Hoo Lee** (37.56) was excluded due to the difficulty of navigating a matchup against Kyle Harrison. We are proceeding cautiously with **Will Smith**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Lawrence Butler**, all of whom are currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their actual batting orders drop significantly, their daily efficiency scores will be subject to revision. We continue to hold **Cal Raleigh** on the IL, hoping for a return to health to bolster our catching depth alongside our active starters.",
